    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the business-day rule in `DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate.java` so the registration date now rolls past public holidays in addition to weekends.\n\n**What changed** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate.java`):\n\n- Added the fixed public-holiday set: `2026-01-01`, `2026-01-26`, `2026-04-25`, `2026-12-25`, `2026-12-28`.\n- Replaced the fixed weekend-only offset logic with a loop that rolls forward one day at a time while the date is a Saturday, Sunday, **or** a listed holiday \u2014 so a date landing on a holiday (even one adjacent to a weekend, like the `2026-12-25`/`2026-12-28` cluster) advances to the next genuine non-holiday weekday.\n- Updated the class Javadoc to reflect the holiday behavior.\n\nThis matches the test's `toBusinessDay` reference implementation in `AcceptanceBase.java`, which enumerates the same holiday table and the same roll-forward algorithm. `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass.",
