    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a clean, additive extension of the existing business-day rule:\n\n- Logic stays in the right unit. `toBusinessDay` already owned the weekend-roll rule; extending it to skip holidays is the natural home, and the two `if` branches collapse cleanly into a single `while` loop that generalizes \"roll forward until the date is a business day.\" No new class or method was needed, and none was invented.\n- No duplication. The weekend and holiday conditions share one loop and one `plusDays(1)` step rather than being special-cased separately.\n- `HOLIDAYS` is a `private static final Set` used only by `toBusinessDay` and placed right above it, with a doc comment stating its purpose. For a fixed, spec-mandated list this is the idiomatic representation.\n- The class Javadoc was updated to match the new behavior, so the class-level contract stays accurate \u2014 a maintainer reading it won't be surprised.\n- No responsibility creep: the class already owned the \"default + business-day-adjust registration date\" concern, and holiday-skipping is squarely within that.\n\nMinor, non-blocking observations (not worth requesting changes): the constant sits between two methods rather than at the top with other fields, and the Javadoc rewrap left a stranded \"The\" at the end of line 14 \u2014 both cosmetic.",
